  "about": "A generic plan for building and launching a small SaaS product with Claude Code as the AI coding assistant: what such a project needs regardless of the product. Three stages: validation and foundations (including the Claude Code setup: CLAUDE.md, permissions, hooks, custom commands), the MVP with a private beta, then billing, legal and public launch. Human review of AI-written code is planned as a task in every stage. Running costs for the first 6 months are under opex, in USD. The top of the tree is split into stages (milestones), and every stage has the same four phases: Analysis, Implementation, Tests and Deployment, so each stage ends with something released and signed off. Every task is estimated in man-days on a T-shirt scale (XS 0.5, S 1, M 3, L 5, XL 10); parents roll up from the tasks below them.",
